      {
        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module checks whether each extracted data column is documented in a codebook or README, and flags documented variables that never appear in the data.",
          "We examined 1 codebook/README/label source and 4 data columns across 1 file.",
          "#### Column Documentation",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## s.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"sleep_hours\", \"id\", \"grp\", \"mood\"), \n    Documented = c(\"conflict\", \"no\", \"yes\", \"yes\"), Label = c(\"NA\", \n    NA, \"Condition\", \"Positive affect\"), \"Codebook Variable\" = c(\"sleep_hours\", \n    NA, \"grp\", \"mood\"), Source = c(\"README.md\", NA, \"README.md\", \n    \"README.md\"), Status = c(\"ambiguous_experiment\", \"unlabelled\", \n    \"labelled\", \"labelled\")), row.names = c(NA, 4L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Conflicting or Ambiguous Definitions\n\n1 matched column has more than one codebook definition, or a definition scoped to a different experiment. These are matched to a codebook but need manual resolution before the label can be trusted.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"s.csv\", Column = \"sleep_hours\", \"Conflicting Labels\" = \"NA\", \n    Sources = \"README.md\", Issue = \"ambiguous_experiment\"), row.names = 3L, class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "LLM model 'mock/rv' reviewed ambiguous cases (parsed 1 file, matched 0 columns, merged 0 labels)."
        ]
